Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:18:02

Fixed. Nexus Release Tool's Commit step works again: it runs tools/fix-modes.sh after git add, and the script did not
come back with the other tools when the suite got its own tooling again ("tools/fix-modes.sh: No such file or
directory"). It is back, and marks every .sh executable in the git index. Six scripts were not executable, in the
working tree or in git: tools/git-setup.sh (the tool's pull runs it first, and would have stopped there),
tools/ci-qt-libs.sh, tools/installer-tests/clb.sh and the install.sh of Fan Control, System Overlay and HDMI CEC
Manager, which a release's ./install.sh needs. They are now.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:05:30

Breaking. The suite stands on its own again, with its own tooling (owner, 13-11-2026: the repository is and stays
standalone; the entry below, the tools taken from a Nexus checkout, is undone). Back in the repository: the tools in
tools/ (apply_design.py, app_tour.py, build_release.py, check_versions.py, ci-local.sh, ci-qt-libs.sh, git-setup.sh,
stage_app.py, suites.py, tag-release.sh, tour_frames.py, the design panel and the disclaimer hook) with their tests,
the CHANGELOG merge driver and check, and the development apps in dev/. ci.yml checks out this repository alone
again, and tests Fan Control, System Overlay and HDMI CEC Manager with the other apps; release.yml and NEXUS_REF are
gone: a release is built and published with tools/tag-release.sh, as before. The wiki builds with the repository's
own hooks, and every address names this repository: github.com/RobertoTorino/bazzite-console for the releases, and
robertotorino.github.io/bazzite-console/ for the wiki. The installer tests stage with the repository's own
tools/stage_app.py. CLAUDE.md describes the standalone repository. What the entry below fixed stays: the addresses
that did not exist, the three apps' wiki chapters, installer tests and lines in the lists, the Media cards out of
the wiki and the README, Bazzite Test's installer test, the "Changes the board" comparison and Bazzite Test's pin.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 20:18:54

Breaking. The suite uses the Nexus tools from Nexus and keeps no copy of them (owner, 13-11-2026: one repository per
suite, the tooling in Nexus). It is worked on inside a Nexus checkout, cloned there as bazzite-console/, and every
job of its workflows starts with Nexus's action, which checks out Nexus at the commit NEXUS_REF names and this
repository inside it. Removed: the copies of the Nexus tools in tools/ (apply_design.py, app_tour.py,
build_release.py, check_versions.py, ci-local.sh, ci-qt-libs.sh, git-setup.sh, stage_app.py, suites.py,
tag-release.sh, tour_frames.py, the design panel and the disclaimer hook) with their tests, the CHANGELOG merge
driver and check (merge_changelog.py, check_changelogs.py: Nexus has none), the copies of the Nexus apps in dev/ with
their own core, and eight stray files at the root. The suite's own tools stay, and its core stays its own
(core/bazzite_console_core): the Nexus tools bundle it. ci.yml is written again for the Nexus checkout, with a job for
the Nexus tools' tests, and release.yml is new (a release commit started by hand, or a tag); a release is built by
GitHub, no longer by tag-release.sh on this machine. The wiki takes the Nexus tools' hooks and is published by
Nexus's docs.yml at robertotorino.github.io/nexus/bazzite-console-suite/. New at the root: CLAUDE.md and NEXUS_REF;
.gitattributes is Nexus's.

Fixed. Every address named github.com/RobertoTorino/nexus-console and robertotorino.github.io/nexus-console, which
do not exist: the repository is RobertoTorino/bazzite-console (the core's SUITE_REPO_URL, where the apps and the
portal look for releases; the READMEs' badges; the wiki). Fan Control, System Overlay and HDMI CEC Manager, listed in
portal/apps.toml, now have their wiki chapter, their installer test and their line in the README, the wiki's app list
and its categories. The wiki and the README no longer describe Media cards: the portal has none. The installer
tests stage with the Nexus tools; Bazzite Test's and the release test expect the app in /opt, where its installer
puts it. tools/check_manifest.py compares a "Changes the board" box with the manifest's text whatever its line
breaks. portal/apps.toml names Bazzite Test's next release, ps5-bazzite-v0.2.0, its VERSION (owner, 13-11-2026).
